Z||000003||PBJ||07-01-2001||08:50 PM||||the ses light comming on tells us that the ecm is getting power or not getting power. During bulb check. soooo.  if in bulb check or when key is on and engine is not running the ses light is not on than the bulb is either burnt out (never seen before) or the ecm does not have power, that is why or could be why you have no fuel pump operation.<P>I'm sorry did you say v6 or 4||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierodude||07-01-2001||08:52 PM||||v6 do i need to change the ecm box? if so does the 85gt box work?<P>------------------<BR>slice the rice! it dosen't pay to drive jap - crap!||||reg||1
Z||000005||PBJ||07-01-2001||11:38 PM||||Check the fusible link located rh frt of engine compartment near battery.  Give them a firm tug to be sure they are not open within.  Check to see if you have battery voltage at the bolt up terminal there too.<P>Access ecm and check for battery voltage on terminals b1 c2 and c16 c1  both are orange wires.  If ok feed. check ground is blk/wht wire terminal d1 c1,<P>again hope this helps.<BR>||||reg||1
